Design reference
----------------
This project is a systemd-based re-expression of NVIDIA NVRC
(https://github.com/NVIDIA/nvrc, Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) NVIDIA CORPORATION).
NVRC's behaviour (boot sequence, kernel parameters, mode detection, fail-fast
semantics, process arguments) is the specification that nvsystemd follows. No NVRC
source code is copied; the behaviour was reimplemented as systemd unit files and a
small C helper. NVRC is also built, unmodified, as the benchmark baseline.

Third-party components (NOT redistributed in this repository)
-------------------------------------------------------------
* systemd (https://systemd.io) as packaged by Fedora, LGPL-2.1-or-later. The image
  build scripts copy /usr/lib/systemd/systemd, systemd-executor and the shared
  libraries they need from the build host at image build time. Those files are
  never committed.
* The Linux kernel used for tests is taken from the host (/lib/modules/*/vmlinuz)
  and is not committed either.
* fixture/fakepci/fakepci.py implements a subset of the vfio-user wire protocol
  (message layouts cross-checked against the Apache-2.0 rust-vmm vfio_user crate).
